Your `reverse_score` function uses `cat(6 - x, "\n")`, which prints the values to the console instead of returning them. In R, `cat()` returns `NULL` (invisibly), so `reverse_score(c(1,2,3,4,5))` evaluates to `NULL`, failing both `identical(...)` checks. The `"\n"` also isn't part of the intended numeric result.

Fix: return the computed vector explicitly, e.g.

```r
reverse_score <- function(x) {
  return(6 - x)
}
```

or simply:

```r
reverse_score <- function(x) {
  6 - x
}
```

Either way, avoid `print()`/`cat()` inside the function so it returns `c(5, 4, 3, 2, 1)` for both inputs. (Your `survey_data` reconstruction is correct.)
